m 32 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/42936"} "Andrea Benelli"] " had been the world record holder since 1996. Considered a favorite at the 1996 and 2000 Olympics, he had managed only a single medal, bronze in 1996. The preliminary leader was Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/104818"} "Marko Kemppainen"] ", who was perfect with 125, and led Benelli by one bird. But Benelli shot a 25 possible in the final round to tie Kemppainen and force a shoot-off. In the shoot-off, both missed a target in the second round, but Kemppainen missed another in the third round, giving the gold to Benelli. The 2002 World Champion was Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/43503"} "Harald Jensen"] ". He made the final, surviving two rounds of shoot-offs to get in, but placed sixth with 145 targets."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "Preliminary Shoot-Off 3-7"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {} "Final Shoot-Off 1/2"] [:th {} "Final Shoot-Off 3-5"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1623"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42936"} "Andrea Benelli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "124 (2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "149 (1)"] [:td {} "5 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1413"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/104818"} "Marko Kemppainen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "125 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "149 (2)"] [:td {} "4 (2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {: